      "body": "## Motivation\n\nWith `--context-length 1024`, `/tokenize` and `/v1/tokenize` can report the tokenizer's 131072-token limit, even though the server only accepts 1024. This gives clients the wrong limit. Fixes #41748.\n\n## Modifications\n\nReturn the server's context length in both tokenize endpoints. Add a regression test for text, batched text, and chat messages.\n\n## Accuracy Tests\n\n- Local MLX `TestTokenizeDetokenize`: 6 passed with a 1024-token server limit.\n- CPU checks with smaller, larger, and unlimited tokenizer limits: 6 passed; token IDs unchanged.\n- `pre-commit run --all-files` passed with Rust-only hooks skipped (no Rust changes). CUDA/AMD tests are pending CI.\n\n## Speed Tests and Profiling\n\nNot applicable; only response metadata changes.\n\n## Checklist\n\n- [x] Added regression coverage and followed the SGLang code style.\n- [x] Documentation and model accuracy/speed benchmarks are not applicable to this response field change.\n\n<!-- pr-states:start -->\n---\n### CI States\n\nLatest PR Test (Base): <!-- slot:pr-test:start -->:x: [Run #36649724528](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/36649724528)<!-- slot:pr-test:end -->\nLatest PR Test (Extra): <!-- slot:pr-test-extra:start -->:x: [Run #36649724188](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/36649724188)<!-- slot:pr-test-extra:end -->\nLatest PR Test (AMD ROCm 10): <!-- slot:pr-test-amd:start -->:x: [Run #36649724451](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/36649724451)<!-- slot:pr-test-amd:end -->\n<!-- pr-states:end -->",
